{"term":"wreck","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:80f5e28c3e1342420f","definition":"Something or someone that has been ruined.","example":"He was an emotional wreck after the death of his wife.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["basket case, mess"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["car wreck","catch wreck","nerve-wreck","nervous wreck","shipwreck","train wreck","wreck car","wreck grab","wreck havoc","wreck of the Hesperus","wreck shop","wreck yard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3907401027b5dee0ae","definition":"The remains of something that has been severely damaged or worn down.","example":"To the fair haven of my native home, / The vvreck of vvhat I was, fatigued I come, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["crash","ruins"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["car wreck","catch wreck","nerve-wreck","nervous wreck","shipwreck","train wreck","wreck car","wreck grab","wreck havoc","wreck of the Hesperus","wreck shop","wreck yard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ac6b42bde388b0ad64","definition":"An event in which something is damaged through collision.","example":"Hard and obſtinate, / As is a rocke amidſt the raging floods: / gaynſt vvhich a ſhip of ſuccour deſolate, / doth ſuffer vvreck both of her ſelfe and goods.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["crash","ruins"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["car wreck","catch wreck","nerve-wreck","nervous wreck","shipwreck","train wreck","wreck car","wreck grab","wreck havoc","wreck of the Hesperus","wreck shop","wreck yard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"h